      "result": "The `status` command is in, tested, and committed on `feat-b` as `7ffe60b`. The full suite passes: 12 tests, the 11 existing plus one new one. I did not merge anything.\n\n- **Command:** `python -m tinytasks.cli status` prints `<N> tasks, <M> overdue`. The total comes from `load_all()` and the overdue count reuses `get_overdue_tasks()`, so it uses the same \"due before now\" rule as `overdue`.\n- **Test:** `test_cli_status_prints_total_and_overdue` in `tests/test_api.py` creates three tasks, one already overdue, and checks the output is `3 tasks, 1 overdue`.\n- **README:** I added the command to the CLI list. This wasn't in the request; say if you'd rather drop it.\n\n**CLAUDE.md:** this branch has no CLAUDE.md. The only copy is on `feat-a` (commit fc83f85). It says any new command that writes a due date must round it down to a whole minute, but `status` only reads due dates, so the rule doesn't apply here. I didn't copy the file onto `feat-b`. If the team expects it on every branch, that's a separate change for whoever owns that convention.",
